  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A coil consisting of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"40\"></span> turns of wire has a cross-sectional area of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0 \\times 10^{-4} \\text{ m}^2\"></span>. The coil is placed in a uniform magnetic field such that its plane is perpendicular to the field lines. The magnetic flux density is then decreased from <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.60 \\text{ T}\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.10 \\text{ T}\"></span> during a time interval of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.20 \\text{ s}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the magnitude of the average electromotive force (emf) induced in the coil?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.3 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{ V}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.0 \\times 10^{-2} \\text{ V}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0 \\times 10^{-2} \\text{ V}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.5 \\times 10^{-1} \\text{ V}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
